From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Draw a clean or sharp desktop picture straight from the XFB
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host presentation option (desktop output only).

The desktop picture went through two resamples: the desktop shader drew the
XFB into a VI-signal-sized texture (720x480), which was then stretched linearly
into the window. On top of that the display copy applies the game's vertical
flicker filter (the 16-32-16 weights of the TV render modes), which on a
progressive desktop display only softens the picture.

AuroraVIOutputConfig gains desktop_picture. SIGNAL (zero, the default for every
existing caller) keeps the previous path unchanged. SMOOTH and SHARP draw the
desktop picture at the window viewport's own size in one pass from the XFB:
the desktop shader maps each window pixel back to signal and source pixels,
so the final copy into the viewport is 1:1. SHARP keeps each source pixel
flat and blends only over about one window pixel at its edge. Both also skip
the display copy's flicker filter by keeping the filter's total weight on the
current row, so brightness and the hardware's /64 rounding stay the same.

The physical VI signal, presented geometry and pointer mapping are unchanged.
Apply after 0073.
